      "extract": "Many known knot and link invariants, including Alexander [@A] and Jones [@J] polynomials, can be obtained from $R$-matrices, solutions to the Yang-Baxter equation (YBE) [@Y; @B1]. Remarkably, many $R$-matrices in turn appear in quantum 3-dimensional Chern-Simons (CS) theory as partition functions of a 3-manifold with boundary, and with properly chosen Wilson lines [@W1]. The corresponding knot invariant acquires an",
      "extractCut": true
